# Every secret and metered key this deployment needs, in one file.
#
#   cp devnet/.env.example devnet/.env && chmod 600 devnet/.env
#   $EDITOR devnet/.env
#
# `devnet/.env` is gitignored, this file is not, so never put a live value here.
#
# It sits beside the scripts rather than inside `devnet/.state/`, because `make stop` deletes
# that directory. Nothing you type here is lost to a teardown.
#
# Two readers, so the syntax is the intersection of both: `KEY=value`, `#` comments, quotes
# around anything containing a space, and no `export`.
#   - `devnet/scripts/lib.sh` sources it, so every numbered script sees these.
#   - `teeism-relayer.service` names it as its EnvironmentFile.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- required

# Pays for every EVM deployment and every relayer submission, on all three chains. Needs
# Sepolia, Arbitrum Sepolia and Base Sepolia ETH.
#
# Keep the `0x`. The scripts accept it either way, but systemd hands this to the relayer
# verbatim and does no normalising of its own.
EVM_PRIVATE_KEY=0x

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- optional

# The 24 words the chain's genesis accounts derive from, and the phrase to import into Keplr:
# account 0 is the funded one.
#
# Leave it empty and `make init` generates one and writes it back into `devnet/.env`. Keeping
# it means the address a wallet already imported still holds funds after the chain is rebuilt;
# losing it means every genesis mints fresh keys and that wallet goes empty.
CELESTIA_MNEMONIC=

# A Sepolia archive endpoint for the Ethereum-origin route, as an Alchemy key.
#
# The relayer proves the origin merkle tree at the ISM's trusted height, which is a finalized
# block, around seventy behind head. Every free Sepolia endpoint measured serves `eth_getProof`
# for the head block alone, so the read that matters is always outside the window. Without a
# key here the route cannot read state proofs and every scan fails.
#
# Set SEPOLIA_ARCHIVE instead if your endpoint is not Alchemy; it wins over this.
ALCHEMY_API_KEY=

# The Base L2 archive key, and the one metered endpoint this deployment genuinely needs.
#
# Base origin calls `eth_getProof` roughly 220k blocks back, the five day dispute window.
# Every free endpoint refuses with "distance to target block exceeds maximum permitted", and
# Base's own RPC does not serve the method at all. A free Alchemy tier is enough.
#
# Nothing reads this automatically. You paste it into the `l2_rpc` field of the
# `base-to-celestia` route in `coprocessor.toml`, and nowhere else: `archive_rpc` must never
# be a metered key, because a large `eth_getLogs` sweep there exhausts the tier and backs off
# every route at once.
ALCHEMY_BASE_KEY=
